## 1. Introduction

Tokenization is one of the fundamental preprocessing steps in Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Generative AI. It is the process of breaking input text into smaller units called tokens, which can be words, subwords, or individual characters.

Language models cannot directly understand raw text. Therefore, tokenizers convert text into tokens and map those tokens to numerical IDs that can be processed by machine learning models.

Different tokenization techniques use different strategies to divide text. This experiment explores three widely used approaches: Byte Pair Encoding (BPE), WordPiece, and SentencePiece.

The experiment compares their tokenization behavior across three languages: English, Telugu, and Hindi.

## 2. Aim

To implement and compare BPE, WordPiece, and SentencePiece tokenization techniques using pretrained language models and analyze their token representations, token IDs, and token counts for English, Telugu, and Hindi text.

