## 12. Observations

The experiment helps demonstrate the following:

1. Different tokenizers may divide the same sentence into different numbers of tokens.
2. Common words may be represented as complete tokens, while unfamiliar words may be divided into subword units.
3. Multilingual tokenizers are designed to process text from multiple writing systems.
4. Token IDs provide the numerical representation required by language models.
5. Tokenization choices can affect the sequence length and representation of multilingual input.

